---
source: crates/cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: result.stdout
---
Audit the rules of a rule set, decision table, bundle or rule

Usage: cleanrules audit [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>
          The document's file, or - for standard input

Options:
      --syntax <SYNTAX>
          Its syntax; by default, from the file's suffix (.json, .yaml, .yml, .rules, .csv), and json for standard input

          Possible values:
          - json: JSON
          - yaml: YAML
          - text: The rule syntax
          - csv:  CSV, for decision tables

      --format <FORMAT>
          What to write

          Possible values:
          - text: Text for people
          - json: The JSON document, on one line
          
          [default: text]

      --fail-on <SEVERITY>
          Exit with 1 when a diagnostic has this severity or a more serious one

          Possible values:
          - error:   Errors only
          - warning: Warnings and errors
          - info:    Any diagnostic
          - never:   Never: exit with 0 whatever the audit finds
          
          [default: error]

      --max-terms <N>
          The most boxes of one node's description (audit limit max_terms) [default: 256]

      --max-steps <N>
          The most steps of the whole audit (audit limit max_steps) [default: 1000000]

      --ruleset-digest
          Carry the rule set digest of the rules audited in the JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Exit codes:
  0  done, nothing found at or above --fail-on
  1  findings at or above --fail-on (audit)
  2  usage error
  3  a file could not be read or written, a document did not read, or the
     operation is not supported for it

Specification: https://github.com/cleanrules/cleanrules/blob/main/spec/cli.md
